    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Factors influencing industrial location",
      "text": "Industrial location is a decision about where an activity can obtain inputs, carry out production and reach users under suitable conditions. Raw materials, labour, energy, capital, transport, markets and site characteristics can all influence that decision. Their importance differs among industries and stages. A fish-processing plant needing rapid access to perishable catch faces a different balance from a service delivered digitally. A useful explanation identifies a factor, shows how it affects operation or cost and connects that effect to the location. A list of factor names alone does not explain attraction to a place.",
      "claim_ids": [
