      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Raw materials matter through availability, quality, perishability, weight and the amount required. A plant processing fish can benefit from proximity to reliable landing points because the catch needs prompt handling and suitable temperature control. Shorter journeys can reduce delays or handling risks, although refrigeration and logistics can extend the feasible distance. A bulky raw material may make transport costs important, while an input available widely may be less decisive. Proximity is therefore a conditional advantage, not proof that the closest site is automatically the best overall choice.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-01-1",
