      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-03",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A supplier’s reliability matters as well as its distance. A nearby landing point with highly uncertain supply may not sustain a plant sized for continuous operation. Seasonal availability can affect how much capacity is used and whether storage or product flexibility is needed. The resource itself must remain biologically and legally available; a factory cannot assume unrestricted catches simply because boats operate nearby. Connecting raw-material location to the plant therefore requires both access and a feasible continuing supply. The decision interacts with fisheries management rather than standing outside it.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-01-1",
