    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Labour influences location through numbers, skills, reliability, training needs and the conditions under which people work. Processing may need workers for handling, machinery operation, maintenance, quality control, administration and logistics. A port town with relevant experience and training can attract an activity that needs those capabilities. Lower wage rates alone do not establish the lowest effective cost if turnover, skill shortages or poor working arrangements reduce productivity. A sound explanation links the particular labour requirement to the task, instead of using cheap labour as a universal answer for every industry.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-01-1",
