    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-05",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Labour supply can also change over time as related firms cluster and training develops. An existing concentration of skills may reduce recruitment difficulty, while growing demand can create competition for experienced workers. The same cluster can therefore provide benefits and pressures. A location account should specify the mechanism supported by the evidence. If a resource identifies a training centre and available technicians, those are relevant details; the mere existence of a large population does not prove that all required skills are present. Population size and occupational suitability are different pieces of information.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
