    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Energy supply can also affect the design of the operation. Backup generation, insulation, efficient equipment or storage arrangements may reduce some exposure to interruption, but they require investment and maintenance. Their presence does not make the supply problem disappear automatically. A location comparison should consider whether the plant can afford and operate the proposed response. A statement that the town has electricity is less informative than evidence about a suitable connection, capacity and reliability for the intended load. The geographical advantage lies in meeting the actual industrial need.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
