    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-08",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Capital is finance and productive resources needed to establish or expand operations. A plant may require premises, processing lines, refrigeration, vehicles, working finance and other investment. Access to suitable finance can make a location or project feasible, while financing costs and repayment conditions affect the decision. The existence of a bank does not guarantee that a borrower will receive a loan. A lender considers the proposal and risk under its own conditions. A supported explanation therefore says that financial services can facilitate investment, not that they must fund every business nearby.",
