    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Working finance is important between paying for inputs and receiving sales income. A fish processor may need to buy catch, pay wages and energy bills and package products before customers pay. Insufficient liquidity can interrupt production even when machinery and a building already exist. This is different from the long-term fixed investment in a plant. A location with suitable financial and business services may help manage both needs, but the firm still requires a viable operation. Geography links access to services with the practical chain rather than promising that finance creates demand or fish stocks by itself.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
