    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Transport connects raw-material sources, the plant and markets. Roads, ports, shipping services and appropriate vehicles influence time, reliability and cost. Perishable or frozen products may need a maintained cold chain, so the suitability of transport matters as much as the number of routes. A short distance with frequent delays can be less useful than a somewhat longer dependable connection. A site comparison should therefore consider the product’s handling requirements, route capacity and services. A line on a map does not prove that transport is affordable or suitable for every cargo.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
