    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Ports can concentrate landing, storage, shipping and supporting services. Walvis Bay and Lüderitz provide Namibian contexts for examining the fishing chain. Lüderitz harbour serves as a base for the fishing industry, and Walvis Bay has cold-storage facilities at the port. These facts support specific links between industrial activity and infrastructure. They do not establish that every plant in either town has identical costs or access, and changing capacity figures need dated sources. The example should explain why the infrastructure matters rather than rely on the place name alone.",
      "claim_ids": [
