    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-13",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Market access can include information and services that connect sellers and buyers. Marketing, distribution networks and compliance with the relevant product requirements can affect whether goods are accepted. These are operational considerations rather than a guarantee that exports will be sold. A location explanation can link a port and specialist services to access to foreign buyers while recognising transport costs, competition and quality requirements. If the resource supplies a local-versus-export comparison, use its product and delivery information instead of assuming that all fish products must serve the same market.",
      "claim_ids": [
