    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-16",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Consider a plant choosing between A beside the landing harbour with reliable power but limited expansion space, and B farther inland with more land but a longer refrigerated journey. A has raw-material and transport-time advantages, while B offers a site-expansion benefit. The decision depends on scale, cold-chain cost, supply and the importance of future growth. A recommendation should compare the stated trade-off rather than declare the closest site best simply because fish are perishable. If costs are supplied, calculate comparable totals and keep assumptions about volume and time explicit.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
