    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-17",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A second comparison can hold market distance similar but identify a skilled maintenance cluster at A and repeated equipment-repair delays at B. The labour/service link can favour A because breakdown time affects production and refrigeration. This is a developed explanation of attraction, not just a list of jobs. If the resource shows higher rent at A, that cost also matters. A cluster advantage can be worthwhile without making the location cheaper on every individual item. Evaluate the combined operational effect using the criterion supplied.",
