      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-19",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "These factors connect industry to the physical environment, settlement, energy, water and trade. The most useful answer is a chain: identify the specific input or service, explain how access affects production or delivery, and connect that effect to the location under the stated conditions. Real decisions involve several such chains and trade-offs. A plant can be close to fish yet lack a suitable site, or near a market yet face unreliable power. A supported judgement uses the evidence to rank relevant needs rather than naming all factors with no explanation of their practical importance.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-1",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-2",
        "CL-6137-2.1.02-01-1",
