      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.1.02-21",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The comparison needs a common period, output and scope. Adding A's monthly energy bill to B's annual delivery cost would produce a meaningless ranking. A site purchase price is also not directly comparable with one month's operating bill without a stated method. If B has essential expansion space that A lacks, that non-cost constraint may matter more than the partial monthly saving. The answer should preserve the calculation and then evaluate what it does and does not resolve. A numerical advantage is evidence within the decision, not permission to ignore feasibility or omitted costs.",
      "claim_ids": [
